          "type": "singleCorrect",
          "level": 2,
          "question": {
            "text": "Element 'B' forms ccp structure and 'A' 'occupies half of the octahedral voids, while oxygen atoms occupy all the tetrahedral voids. The structure of bimetallic oxide is :",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "ZXJNm",
              "text": "$\\mathrm{A}_{2} \\mathrm{BO}_{4}$",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "aBgHN",
              "text": "$\\mathrm{AB}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{4}$",
              "isCorrect": true,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "3rTDj",
              "text": "$\\mathrm{A}_{2} \\mathrm{~B}_{2} \\mathrm{O}$",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "dx7wl",
              "text": "$\\mathrm{A}_{4} \\mathrm{~B}_{2} \\mathrm{O}$",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "No. of lattice points $=$ No. of octahedral voids $=\\frac{1}{2} \\times$ No. of tetrahedral\r\n\r\nvoids in $c c p$ structure\r\n\r\n$\\therefore$ No. of atoms of $B=4$\r\n\r\nNo. of atoms of $A=\\frac{1}{2} \\times$ No. of octahedral voids\r\n\r\n$=\\frac{1}{2} \\times 4=2$\r\n\r\nNo. of atoms of $O=$ All tetrahedral voids $=2 \\times$ No. of lattice points\r\n\r\n$=2 \\times 4=8$\r\n\r\nHence, $A: B: O=1: 2: 4$\r\n\r\nTherefore, the formula of the compound is $A B_{2} O_{4}$",
            "image": null
          },
          "videoSolution": null,
