          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "<p>Ionic solids are formed by three dimensional arrangements of positive charged ions i.e. cations and negative charged ions i.e. anions. These ions are held together by coulombic(electrostatic) forces and hence, ionic solids are hard and brittle.</p><p>Ionic solids have highest melting point due to strong electrostatic force of attraction.</p>",
