          "question": {
            "text": "A metallic element has a cubic lattice. Each edge of the unit cell is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>.</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;and the density of metal is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>. The unit cell in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of metal are",
