          "type": "singleCorrect",
          "level": 3,
          "question": {
            "text": "An elemental crystal has a density of $8570 \\mathrm{~kg} / \\mathrm{m}^{3}$. The packing efficiency is 0.68 . The closest distance of approach between neighbouring atom is $2.86 Ã…$. What is the mass of one atom approximately?",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "7AIyD",
              "text": "$93 \\mathrm{amu}$",
              "isCorrect": true,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "al9L0",
              "text": "$39 \\mathrm{amu}$",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "Dibo1",
              "text": "$63 \\mathrm{amu}$",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "PVwGt",
              "text": "$29 \\mathrm{amu}$",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "The packing efficiency $=0.68$, means the given lattice is $\\mathrm{BCC}$. The closest distance of approach $=2 \\mathrm{r}$\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\n\\begin{array}{l}\r\n\r\n2 r=2.86 A=a \\sqrt{3} \\\\\r\n\r\n\\text { or a }=\\frac{2 \\times 2.86}{\\sqrt{3}}=3.30 Ã…\r\n\r\n\\end{array}\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\nLet atomic weight of the element $=\\mathrm{a}$\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\n\\begin{aligned}\r\n\r\n\\therefore & \\frac{2 \\times 9}{36 \\times 10^{23} \\times(3.3)^{3} \\times 10^{-24}}=8.57 \\\\\r\n\r\n\\mathrm{a} &=8.57 \\times 3 \\times(3.3)^{3} \\times 0.1 \\\\\r\n\r\n&=92.39 \\simeq 93 \\mathrm{amu}\r\n\r\n\\end{aligned}\r\n\r\n$$",
            "image": null
          },
