            }
          ],
          "type": "singleCorrect",
          "level": 2,
          "question": {
            "text": "In a compound, atoms of elements <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi></math> form ccp lattice and those of element <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math> occupy <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>rd</mi></math>&nbsp;of&nbsp;tetrahedral voids. The formula of the compound can be",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "0lQYi",
              "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>",
              "isCorrect": true,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "9CnsR",
              "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "LBwBf",
              "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi></math>",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "2zDbf",
              "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "<p>Let atoms of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi></math> in ccp structure <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></math></p><p>Then, number of tetrahedral voids <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8757;</mo></math> Number of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math> atoms <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math> rd of tetrahedral voids</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> Number of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math> atoms <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>200</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>400</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Hence, formula of compound can be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>.</p>",
            "image": null
